DXVK patch 09 -- fail closed on a null D3D9 factory and expose WSI priming failure.

Apply after dxvk-patches/02-d3d8-wine-user-driver-init.patch to DXVK-Sarek
commit 617958fe1cf2b10e06fa751d3e40bd765dcf2cc6. This is a source-only audit
candidate; it is not part of either production DLL stage.

Patch 02 already turns missing d3d9.dll and a missing Direct3DCreate9 export
into DxvkError. Complete that boundary for the legal factory-null result rather
than dereferencing address zero in D3D8Interface's constructor. Keep the hidden
window attempt non-fatal for compatibility, but make its failure visible in the
existing cold-start d3d8 log instead of silently continuing into an
unattributable missing-WSI-extension failure.

Neither branch is reached after a successful FINALPLAY21 cold start. There is
no per-frame code or performance claim.

--- a/src/d3d8/d3d8_interface.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d8/d3d8_interface.cpp
@@ -18,7 +18,11 @@ namespace dxvk {
     if (!createD3D9)
       throw DxvkError("D3D8Interface: ERROR! Direct3DCreate9 not found");
 
-    return createD3D9(D3D_SDK_VERSION);
+    auto d3d9 = createD3D9(D3D_SDK_VERSION);
+    if (!d3d9)
+      throw DxvkError("D3D8Interface: ERROR! Direct3DCreate9 returned null");
+
+    return d3d9;
   }
 
   D3D8Interface::D3D8Interface()
--- a/src/d3d8/d3d8_main.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d8/d3d8_main.cpp
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@ extern "C" {
       0, 0, 1, 1, nullptr, nullptr, GetModuleHandleW(nullptr), nullptr);
     if (driverWindow)
       DestroyWindow(driverWindow);
+    else
+      dxvk::Logger::warn("D3D8: Failed to create the user-driver priming window");
 
     IDirect3D8* pDirect3D = nullptr;
     dxvk::CreateD3D8(&pDirect3D);
